{
 "id": "t3-fork",
 "title": "A two-word joke about a fork put T3 Code’s telemetry in front of everyone",
 "date": "2026-11-24",
 "summary": "A Chinese-language fork of T3 Code was mistaken for the app. Theo called it a knockoff and “Temu3 Code”. The two settled it the same day; the crowd read the code, and T3 Code changed what it collects.",
 "topics": [
  {
   "id": "forks",
   "angle": "The name, the joke, the crowd and the code."
  }
 ],
 "claims": [
  {
   "text": "Until November 24 T3 Code’s README invited anyone unhappy with it to fork it, with no mention of branding.",
   "who": "the README diff",
   "status": "read",
   "sources": [
    "pr41898"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "DDdxx666 announced T3 Stardust on November 22 as an open-source version anyone may modify, with T3 in its name.",
   "who": "DDdxx666",
   "status": "read",
   "sources": [
    "x-stardust"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Suyuan says the fork’s link was seen in a group chat, described as T3Code.",
   "who": "suyuan1711",
   "status": "said",
   "sources": [
    "x-group"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Suyuan posted a correction at 11:04 UTC on November 23; Theo’s knockoff post is stamped 11:11.",
   "who": "the posts’ timestamps",
   "status": "read",
   "sources": [
    "x-my-fault",
    "x-knockoff"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Theo posted that a Chinese knockoff of T3 Code seemed to be going around, because the app shown was not theirs.",
   "who": "Theo",
   "status": "read",
   "sources": [
    "x-knockoff"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "The maker replied at 11:19 UTC that it was an unofficial, modified version; “Temu3 Code” is stamped 11:22.",
   "who": "the posts’ timestamps",
   "status": "read",
   "sources": [
    "x-unofficial",
    "x-temu3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Theo posted “Temu3 Code” on November 23; defenders call it a pun and critics call it racist.",
   "who": "Theo and others",
   "status": "read",
   "sources": [
    "x-temu3",
    "x-dash",
    "x-bermudi"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Theo told the maker to change the name at once or Theo would ask GitHub to take the account down, and in another reply that forks themselves were fine.",
   "who": "Theo",
   "status": "read",
   "sources": [
    "x-right-now",
    "x-dontmind"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "The maker renamed the project Stardust on November 23 and wrote that Theo liked the name.",
   "who": "DDdxx666",
   "status": "read",
   "sources": [
    "x-renamed",
    "x-cool-name",
    "x-much-better"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "The maker wrote that there is no bad blood with Theo; Theo wrote that the two are good.",
   "who": "DDdxx666 and Theo",
   "status": "said",
   "sources": [
    "x-no-feud",
    "x-good"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "William’s post says 48 minutes separate Theo’s two posts; they are stamped 11:11:49 and 11:22:31 UTC.",
   "who": "the posts’ timestamps",
   "status": "counted",
   "sources": [
    "x-william",
    "x-knockoff",
    "x-temu3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Theo wrote on November 23 that open source stays open source even when a trillion dollar company uses it.",
   "who": "Theo",
   "status": "read",
   "sources": [
    "x-trillion"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Huxpro wrote that MIT licenses the code and neither the name nor the brand.",
   "who": "Huxpro",
   "status": "said",
   "sources": [
    "x-huxpro"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Theo insulted Chinese tech Twitter as a whole and later wrote that it was about the community and not individuals; Chen Dahuang had insulted Theo by name.",
   "who": "both",
   "status": "read",
   "sources": [
    "x-cesspit",
    "x-generalizing",
    "x-scum"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Chen Dahuang’s telemetry post had 1,582,257 views when counted.",
   "who": "X’s count",
   "status": "counted",
   "sources": [
    "x-dahuang"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Analytics were merged in March; the May homepage said no telemetry unless you opt in; a June 18 commit removed the words.",
   "who": "the records",
   "status": "read",
   "sources": [
    "pr174",
    "archive",
    "c3bdaa6e"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "A maintainer wrote in June that opting out would not be made easier, because the project needs to know how many users it has; a later pull request for a switch was closed.",
   "who": "juliusmarminge",
   "status": "read",
   "sources": [
    "i1397",
    "pr27077"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "T3 Code’s analytics read Codex and Claude sign-in files and sent hashes of the ids found there; Theo says no files, prompts or code were received.",
   "who": "the pull request and Theo",
   "status": "read",
   "sources": [
    "pr42299",
    "x-honest"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "A readers’ note under Anthony Ronning’s post says T3 Connect is optional, grants full access by design, and does not relay plaintext session messages.",
   "who": "X readers’ note",
   "status": "said",
   "sources": [
    "x-ronning"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Theo’s first answer to the viral claim insulted the people making it and disputed it on three points.",
   "who": "Theo",
   "status": "read",
   "sources": [
    "x-stupid"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Theo posted that the source would close that night, then posted that it would not.",
   "who": "Theo",
   "status": "read",
   "sources": [
    "x-close",
    "x-wont"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Merged on November 24, and in that evening’s nightly build but no stable release when checked at 23:13 UTC: analytics no longer open provider sign-in files and still link a T3 Connect account, relay traces no longer record IP addresses, and a trademark policy. Mia posted the first of these and called the mission accomplished.",
   "who": "the pull requests and Mia",
   "status": "read",
   "sources": [
    "pr42299",
    "pr42380",
    "pr41898",
    "x-mission",
    "x-changes",
    "c84e4264",
    "nightly"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Theo published 95,789 events, described as all of Theo’s own.",
   "who": "Theo",
   "status": "said",
   "sources": [
    "x-events",
    "x-dump"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "One user says reading auth files crosses a line; another says T3 Code takes far less data than expected.",
   "who": "lyraxana and dagecky",
   "status": "said",
   "sources": [
    "x-lyra",
    "x-dagecky"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Mia lists T3CODE_TELEMETRY_ENABLED=false and T3CODE_OTEL_SDK_DISABLED=true as the off settings.",
   "who": "MiaAI_lab",
   "status": "said",
   "sources": [
    "x-mia",
    "docs"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "DODOREACH published a template data request; sabotaj0707 says a complaint was filed with a German authority.",
   "who": "both",
   "status": "said",
   "sources": [
    "x-gdpr",
    "x-germany"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "T3 Code’s README now says to fork it under your own branding.",
   "who": "the README",
   "status": "read",
   "sources": [
    "readme"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "No finding by any regulator was found on November 24.",
   "who": "our search",
   "status": "open",
   "sources": [
    "x-germany"
   ]
  }
 ],
